  "adjustments": [
    "One zleap.sag package; imports reference its common helpers.",
    "Host supplies account models, local time and medical extraction with entity catalog identity resolution. Extraction performs no historical event recall or query embedding; later event organization and query retrieval remain independent.",
    "SQLite/Lance persistence and append-only evidence stay in Serenita; upstream storage and compact-template fallback are excluded.",
    "Extraction uses only changed fields on updates. JSON Schema, nonempty text and authorized references are validated before append.",
    "Original recursive event traversal is retained. The medical schema allows L0/L1/L2 with full coverage and nonduplicate sibling instructions. Persisted Events contain no nesting metadata; Contains is an additional host relation decided by the relation-stage model after Episode membership.",
    "Long extraction uses the copied SAG chunker and assembler; independently extracts each chunk with previous heading and first 300 characters as metadata, then gathers results in source order. Medical context, serial execution, exact evidence positions, bounded repairs and authorized checkpoints are host adaptations.",
    "Local package, symbols, configuration fields and prompt names use SAG; upstream source paths and source hashes retain their original names and values.",
    "Adopted interfaces exclude unused candidate membership conveniences, parser identity/cache defaults and LLMMessage.to_dict; host callbacks own identity rules and request serialization. Internal orchestration imports utilities directly without changing public package exports."
  ],
